{"schema":"forgedock.run-event/v1","eventId":"ce1591b7-2a45-44ff-85dc-1f70f862a2fc","runId":"b00c651c-419f-40aa-a356-2ab455f1615d","repository":"RapierCraftStudios/forgedock-pi","sequence":8,"previousEventHash":"sha256:5c5911a713a5d3d43ddd20b5f5577838dc9949820ac158a1c1c20f0612c1be1c","type":"phase.completed","actor":{"kind":"extension","sessionId":"01a03d3d-27e2-717f-98de-70dc4102ffe9","leaseEpoch":1},"occurredAt":"2026-08-26T09:10:46.847Z","idempotencyKey":"phase:investigate:1:complete","payload":{"phase":"investigate","attempt":1,"evidence":["Issue #92 reports stale workflow labels while durable phase checkpoints advance.","The committed fix centralizes checkpoint-to-label mapping and covers resolve, build, review, merge, close, and cleanup transitions.","Regression coverage exercises lifecycle mapping and replacement while preserving the bug label."],"report":"<!-- FORGE:INVESTIGATOR -->\n## Investigation Report\n\n**Verdict**: CONFIRMED\n\n### Root Cause\n\nWorkflow label projection was incomplete at phase boundaries. The checkpoint runtime only mapped a subset of starts and investigation completion, leaving durable resolve, review completion, and merge transitions without canonical label reconciliation. Parent-owned merge transitions also relied on terminal cleanup before projecting the merged label.\n\n### Evidence\n\n- `src/agents/child-runtime.ts` delegated checkpoint label selection to a partial mapping.\n- `src/adapters/github-projection.ts` already replaces all prior `workflow:*` labels while preserving unrelated labels.\n- `src/core/artifact-protocol.ts` defines the canonical workflow labels.\n- Commit `83d2d412` adds complete lifecycle mapping, parent merge projection, and regression coverage.\n\n### Acceptance Spec\n\n- Every relevant phase start or completion projects the canonical workflow label.\n- The prior workflow label is removed before the new one is retained.\n- Unrelated labels such as `bug` remain unchanged.\n- Tests cover lifecycle transitions, awaiting-merge, merged, invalid investigation, and label replacement.\n\n<!-- INVESTIGATION:COMPLETE -->"}}
